            <ArticleTitle>Aseptic HLA B27-positive spondylodiscitis: decreased 18F-FDG uptake after etanercept treatment.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>163-165</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.4081/reumatismo.2016.911</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We observed a 69-year old man suffering from HLA B27 ankylosing spondylitis with persistent night back pain. 18F-FDG-PET/CT showed an increased metabolism at the level of the spinal space of L2-L3, L3-L4 with increased uptake compatible with spondylodiscitis. He started therapy with etanercept 50 mg/week. After six months of treatment repeated testing showed no uptake of the discs and vertebral bodies.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
